<title>JAPAN: Hosiden drifts lower on profit taking.</title>
<headline>Hosiden drifts lower on profit taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hosiden Corp shares drifted lower in the Wednesday morning session due to profit taking after going limit-up on Tuesday, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0153 GMT, the shares were down 25 yen at 885 yen.  </p>
<p>&quot;It rose as much as 15 yen early in the morning, but profit-taking pressure was strong, capping gains and then sending it into negative territory,&quot; a broker at a mid-sized brokerage said.</p>
</text>
